github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/darwin_arm64
===============================================

lib/ contains FFmpeg libraries (https://ffmpeg.org) built for darwin_arm64:

  libavcodec.a libavdevice.a libavformat.a libavutil.a libgoffmpeg.dylib libswresample.a libswscale.a

shared/ contains the same FFmpeg built as shared libraries, for apps that
ship it so that a user can replace it (LGPL 2.1 section 6b):

  libavcodec-goffmpeg.63.dylib libavdevice-goffmpeg.63.dylib libavformat-goffmpeg.63.dylib libavutil-goffmpeg.61.dylib libswresample-goffmpeg.7.dylib libswscale-goffmpeg.10.dylib

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
No local patches: goffmpeg's build applies patches/*.patch to the FFmpeg
checkout, and goffmpeg has no such files (BUILDING.md: "The directory is
currently empty").

License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The full
text is in LICENSE at the root of this repository, and is included in this
module's zip by the go command. The build used neither --enable-gpl nor
--enable-nonfree; each library reports "license: LGPL version 2.1 or later".

Configure line of lib/, as recorded in libavutil (avutil_configuration()).

  --prefix=/darwin_arm64 --extra-cflags=-fPIC --enable-pic --disable-autodetect --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --disable-encoders --disable-muxers --disable-avfilter --enable-swscale --enable-swresample --enable-network --arch=arm64 --target-os=darwin --enable-securetransport --enable-videotoolbox --enable-hwaccel='h264_videotoolbox,hevc_videotoolbox,vp9_videotoolbox,av1_videotoolbox' --enable-avdevice --enable-indev=avfoundation --enable-avfoundation --cc='clang -arch arm64 -mmacosx-version-min=11.0' --enable-static --disable-shared

Configure line of shared/, as recorded in its libavutil. It is the line
above with --enable-shared --disable-static and the flags that name and
place the shared libraries.

  --prefix=/darwin_arm64 --extra-cflags=-fPIC --enable-pic --disable-autodetect --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --disable-encoders --disable-muxers --disable-avfilter --enable-swscale --enable-swresample --enable-network --arch=arm64 --target-os=darwin --enable-securetransport --enable-videotoolbox --enable-hwaccel='h264_videotoolbox,hevc_videotoolbox,vp9_videotoolbox,av1_videotoolbox' --enable-avdevice --enable-indev=avfoundation --enable-avfoundation --cc='clang -arch arm64 -mmacosx-version-min=11.0' --enable-shared --disable-static --build-suffix=-goffmpeg --install-name-dir='@rpath'

Corresponding source:
  FFmpeg:  https://github.com/belluikit/ffmpeg/tree/goffmpeg-e2bc6d88cd
           belluikit's mirror of FFmpeg. The tag is commit
           e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a and stays for as long as
           libraries built from it are published.
  Build:   https://github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg (Makefile, BUILDING.md), which
           pins that revision and these configure lines.
  Bridge:  lib/libgoffmpeg.* is goffmpeg's bridge.c and bridge_avf_darwin.m
           (BSD-3-Clause), built by goffmpeg's 'make bridge-shared'. It holds
           no FFmpeg code: it loads the libraries in shared/, looking beside
           itself and in ../shared.
           The current lib/libgoffmpeg.* was built from goffmpeg commit
           56ff0d7 by GitHub Actions run 42614744092.
  Shared:  shared/ was built by goffmpeg's 'make dist-shared' from goffmpeg
           commit 2eb34b5 by GitHub Actions run 42569150705, from the same FFmpeg
           revision and base configure line as lib/.
